 :open-questions
 [{:id :original-broom-finite-reserve
   :cards [:catalog/original-base-k-125-broom]
   :question "How should Broom resolve when fewer than seven undealt minor improvements remain?"
   :current-behavior "Draw every remaining eligible card from the persisted private reserve; never recycle cards discarded during play."
   :status :implementation-assumption
   :sources ["https://agricola.no/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/compendium.pdf"]
   :note "The compendium specifies seven cards and excludes in-game discards but does not resolve reserve exhaustion. Taking the remaining cards is the finite-reserve interpretation."}
  {:id :original-wildlife-reserve-trough
   :cards [:catalog/original-base-i-102-wildlife-reserve :catalog/original-base-e-59-drinking-trough]
   :question "How are Drinking Trough's two additional places distributed on Wildlife Reserve?"
   :current-behavior "Wildlife Reserve keeps its one place per species and gains two flexible places in total, not two per species. Shepherd's Pipe adds two sheep places separately."
   :status :implementation-assumption
   :sources ["https://agricola.no/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/compendium.pdf"]
   :note "The compendium explicitly permits the capacity increase but does not spell out its allocation across species. The total-two interpretation follows Drinking Trough's wording; no explicit designer ruling for this combination was located."}
  {:id :original-ratcatcher-adoption
   :cards [:catalog/original-base-e-198-ratcatcher :revised-base/a092]
   :question "How does Ratcatcher interact with a newborn adopted during rounds ten or twelve?"
   :current-behavior "Ratcatcher suppresses one adult offspring's placement. An adopted newborn becomes eligible if no offspring was already suppressed; guests are excluded. An already suppressed worker remains idle after later family growth."
   :status :implementation-assumption
   :sources ["https://agricola.no/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/compendium.pdf"]}
  {:id :lazy-sowman-empty-sow-action
   :cards [:catalog/revised-artifex-expansion-a-94-lazy-sowman]
   :question "May Lazy Sowman use Grain Utilization solely to decline Sow, without sowing or baking, including when no sowing plan is possible?"
   :current-behavior "A board placement must still perform a legal action. Declining Sow completes Cultivation when a field is plowed, or Grain Utilization when bread is baked; otherwise the uncommitted placement is cancelled. Generic Sow offers without sowing potential are omitted."
   :status :unresolved
   :sources ["https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WUl0HlzX6Yx0ume75UmpaIMhoHukx9XufM_LbV1oZ6E/edit"
             "https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/2108049/article/30659621#30659621"
             "https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/2323856/about-decline-an-action-instead-an-action-or-some"
             "https://www.reedstonefood.com/agricola/compendium"]
   :note "The older mixed-edition compendium permits an empty Bake/Sow action, while community discussion conflicts. The Revised compendium cites Uwe via Ponton for repeated Cultivation, but the linked primary post could not be retrieved. Existing behavior is an interpretation, not a verified designer ruling on empty Sow actions."}
  {:id :fertilizers-and-moldboard-action-boundary
   :cards [:catalog/revised-artifex-expansion-a-73-agricultural-fertilizers :revised-base/b019]
   :question "Does Farmland's field plus Moldboard Plow's additional field count as one action for Agricultural Fertilizers?"
   :current-behavior "The two plow effects are treated separately; one field from each does not grant a Sow action."
   :status :unresolved
   :note "No explicit publisher or designer clarification was found. Do not present either interpretation as a verified ruling."}]
 :regressions
 [{:id :original-k-reed-hut-worker-order
   :cards [:catalog/original-base-k-138-reed-hut :catalog/original-base-i-227-church-warden]
   :source "https://boardgames.stackexchange.com/questions/14935/church-warden-vs-reed-hut-in-round-14" :authority :community-discussion
   :rule "Reed Hut's occupant acts after family and Guest, must be fed and receives no family points until adopted. Another family member must perform adoption; the occupant cannot adopt itself. Church Warden counts actual placements, so adoption that removes the occupant's remaining placement does not create a fifth placement. The discussion cites the compendium; its original publisher-forum links are unavailable."
   :test agricola.original-k-workers-draw-test/reed-hut-is-last-after-family-and-guest-and-cannot-adopt-itself}
  {:id :original-k-broom-private-reserve
   :cards [:catalog/original-base-k-125-broom]
   :source "https://agricola.no/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/compendium.pdf" :authority :unofficial-compilation
   :rule "Broom replaces the owner's remaining minor hand using a private, persisted reserve from the setup's included card packs for all supported player counts. It never reintroduces cards discarded during play and offers a paid, prerequisite-checked extra minor play."
   :test agricola.original-k-workers-draw-test/broom-draws-private-undealt-minors-and-preserves-a-paid-play-window}

